WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.285
Look at a map,

2
00:00:01.285 --> 00:00:02.936
and South America seems to

3
00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.255
fit into Africa.

4
00:00:04.255 --> 00:00:07.090
Alfred Wegener took that seriously.

5
00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:10.313
Wegener proposed continental drift in

6
00:00:10.313 --> 00:00:12.866
1912, with one supercontinent,

7
00:00:12.866 --> 00:00:15.067
Pangaea. In the 1960s,

8
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.843
Harry Hess's sea-floor spreading led

9
00:00:17.843 --> 00:00:19.898
to plate tectonics.

10
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.806
At divergent boundaries,

11
00:00:21.806 --> 00:00:23.043
plates move apart.

12
00:00:23.043 --> 00:00:24.340
At convergent ones,

13
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.271
they collide,

14
00:00:25.271 --> 00:00:27.049
as India did with Asia.

15
00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:28.638
At transform boundaries,

16
00:00:28.638 --> 00:00:30.884
they slide past each other.

17
00:00:31.213 --> 00:00:33.407
Wegener's idea was rejected for

18
00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:35.944
decades, because he couldn't explain

19
00:00:35.944 --> 00:00:38.255
the force that moved continents.

20
00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:40.129
Your turn.

21
00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:42.215
Which type of boundary?
